      "TWA-TRANS WORLD AIRLINES\nBoeing 707-131\nThe 707 ushered TWA into the jet age in 1959, and eventual-\nly flew virtually all of the carrier's routes. During the follow-\ning 25 years, TWA operated 129 707's, more than any other 2\nairline. Eight different models have been involved, from/this\nearly model 131 with transcontinental frange, to the\nadvanced 331B which operated the long honstop polar\nflights. Although N731TW was the first to be painted in TWA\ncolors, it was involved in the airplane's certification program\nand became the eleventh to be delivered, on July 9. 1959\nRetired in 1970, it was later sold.\nDun beone.\nwire in final\n= appranh\nfor Kansas lity. Have had\na great day. nish you\nlakove been here.\nUSA 13c\nCrazy Horse\n, Inc., P.O. Box 188\nBethel\nI, Conn.\n06801 U.S.A.\nPOWERALI\npost caru\nGoorse bayuski\n22 1 стека\nSan Franisco, CA 94114\nthe miami- No. e Ny-chicago e\nChicago- kanses city. Also there was a\nas will wint\nsunday - gove Bobbie\n2001.082.118"
